WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.713
The third mechanism is lifecycle events.

2
00:00:02.713 --> 00:00:06.997
The HR-driven lifecycle itself
belongs to HR-Driven Identity;

3
00:00:06.997 --> 00:00:11.450
this chapter covers only the
workflow tasks that change access.

4
00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:15.162
A joiner gets access through
packages, never a direct add.

5
00:00:15.162 --> 00:00:20.401
A move is a re-derivation, not an extra
grant: the old department's access goes,

6
00:00:20.401 --> 00:00:25.049
the new department's arrives, and
anything left over goes to review.

7
00:00:25.049 --> 00:00:29.837
A leaver loses every package, every
group, and their refresh tokens.

8
00:00:29.837 --> 00:00:32.600
An inactivity workflow catches accounts

9
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:35.600
whose HR record never
produced a leaver event.

10
00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.006
Guests are where unreviewed
access piles up fastest,

11
00:00:39.006 --> 00:00:42.800
because nobody's HR record ends
when a partner project does.

12
00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:46.575
So guests arrive through a package
with a sponsor and an expiry.

13
00:00:46.575 --> 00:00:50.901
All of this needs Entra ID Governance
licensing for the whole workforce,

14
00:00:50.901 --> 00:00:52.820
or some people stay ungoverned.
